win32: include synchapi.h from windows.h

SRWLOCK and the SRW lock functions are declared in synchapi.h, but windows.h
never includes that header, so a translation unit that only includes
<windows.h> cannot name SRWLOCK. SQLite 3.54.0 uses SRWLOCK in its mutex
implementation, so its amalgamation fails to compile under tcc with
"';' expected (got 'SRWLOCK')".

Include synchapi.h from windows.h directly after winbase.h, as the other
kernel32 sub-headers are pulled in. synchapi.h is self-guarded and gates its
Vista-only prototypes on _WIN32_WINNT, so including it adds no new symbols
for default builds.
diff --git a/win32/include/winapi/windows.h b/win32/include/winapi/windows.h
index ff6454a..d64516e 100644
--- a/win32/include/winapi/windows.h
+++ b/win32/include/winapi/windows.h
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@
 
 #include <windef.h>
 #include <winbase.h>
+#include <synchapi.h>
 #include <wingdi.h>
 #include <winuser.h>
 #include <winnls.h>
